23,"team":"LAC","distance":0.7925,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Kellen Moore"}],"defense":[{"season":2019,"team":"ARI","distance":0.65,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2021,"team":"JAX","distance":0.6642,"shared":18,"play_caller":null},{"season":2021,"team":"DET","distance":0.6671,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Aaron Glenn"},{"season":2021,"team":"ARI","distance":0.7229,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2019,"team":"WAS","distance":0.7288,"shared":18,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Buccaneers went 8-9 in 2022 and were outscored 358 to 313. The defense did most of the work, finishing 12th in EPA allowed while the offense ranked 22nd in EPA per play. Their most distinctive traits were the highest pass rate and the most defenders in the box in the league.","offense":"The Buccaneers offense was a little below average by EPA per play, and it was much better passing the ball than running it. They threw more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score did not call for it. Schematically, they stood out for the 2nd lowest play-action rate and the 3rd lowest empty formation usage in the league. Tom Brady ran the passing game, with Chris Godwin leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Buccaneers defense was a little above average by EPA allowed per play. Its strongest area was success rate allowed, where it ranked 10th, and its weakest was pressure rate, where it ranked 27th. Shaquil Barrett was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was Vita Vea, who had 6.5 sacks despite playing only 59% of the snaps. Schematically, they had the most defenders in the box in the league.","special":"The Buccaneers were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 82% of field goals, which was well below average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 22% of the money on the books. Their quarterbacks were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Tom Brady played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,694 yards. Targets were spread around, with Chris Godwin and Mike Evans leading a group where nobody took more than a fifth of the looks. The backfield was a committee led by Leonard Fournette and Rachaad White. On defense, Vita Vea led the team with 6.5 sacks and Jamel Dean picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"This staff is not in the coaching data, so the comparisons below are based on scheme alone. Their offense looked most like the 2024 Seahawks and the 2025 Jaguars under Liam Coen. Their defense looked most like the 2019 Cardinals under Vance Joseph and the 2021 Jaguars.","trends":"The offense went from 2nd in EPA per play in 2021 to 22nd in 2022, a big step back. The defense moved from 4th in EPA allowed per play in 2021 to 12th in 2022, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 5% to 22%.","notes":"2022 is the first season with every data source available, including FTN's play design charting. It is also the last season that used the older formation labels, so singleback and I formation rates still appear here."}}